WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.670
Fierce Battle!  Battle City Begins

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.580
Yugi's light was on all night.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.660
He must've pulled an all-nighter to build his deck for today's tournament.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:48.820
I know!

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.550
I'll go watch Yugi duel for the first time in awhile!

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.660
I'll invite Anzu!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.570
Okay, it's ready.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.220
Ahh!  It's already morning!

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.070
I spent all night deciding whether to include a spell card or not.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.080
Partner...

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.400
There's something I need to tell you before the battle.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.400
What is it?

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:25.160
When we fight in Battle City, I will have to fight to find myself.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.090
Find yourself?

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.600
It's an important fight for me.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.660
But I don't think I can win this fight without your help.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:43.200
I always believe in you and the deck we created together.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.850
Never forget that.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.810
Okay, that's fine.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.320
You're not going to ask for details?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:58.780
I'm fine just knowing that you're fighting for deeper reasons than acquiring rare cards.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:07.060
I won't ask what you're searching for until you're ready to tell me.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.570
I always believe in you and the deck we created together too.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.570
Partner...

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:17.840
Let's go!

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.280
It's no good!

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.620
I don't know how to beat him without Red-Eyes!

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.800
I didn't tell Yugi about that guy's deck because I want to get revenge by myself.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.040
It's too late to ask for his advice.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:43.630
I know!

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.740
I'll have Shizuka cheer me up.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.220
She'll be like, "Go for it, big brother!"

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.960
Hello.  Shizuka Kawai's room.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.940
Who is this?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.660
Who?  Oh, is this Jonouchi?

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.880
It's me, Honda.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.020
Honda?

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.320
Why are you there?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:09.500
Since you're busy with Battle City, I came to see her in your place.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.740
You never told me!

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:17.900
Big brother, Honda was telling me a lot about the cards.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.840
Honda says that he taught you how to play.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:28.240
Thanks to Honda's training, you were able to finish second at Duelist Kingdom.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.760
I hope you try hard so that you can be just like Honda.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.860
Well, that's about it.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.030
Try hard so that you can get Red-Eyes back.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:38.800
Later.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.530
Honda!

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.930
I'm going to kill him!

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.590
Who are they?

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:56.400
I don't know.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.310
They have weird machines on their arms.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.740
You guys don't know?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.050
About what?

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:08.490
Starting today, this city becomes Battle City, a battlefield for Duel Monsters.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.640
Battle City?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.610
Walk on the edge of the sidewalk if you don't want to get hurt.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.710
This plate was included with my Duel Disk.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.340
It shows one section of Domino City.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.000
I heard this was the starting location.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.000
Yugi!

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:37.970
Mai!

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.470
It's finally time, Yugi.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.000
Where's Jonouchi?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.570
He should be here somewhere.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.450
So he is participating!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.590
He's one of the selected duelists!

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:51.090
We meet again, Yugi and Mai!

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.820
Insector Haga and Dinosaur Ryuzaki!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.070
I'll pay you back for Duelist Kingdom!

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.210
Remember that!

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.230
I'm more skilled than before!

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:09.600
My Insect Deck has greatly powered up!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.590
You've come to lose again?

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:16.960
Kajiki!

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.010
Your Insect Deck is a bunch of scrubs.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.590
Scrubs?

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:22.970
That's right!

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:26.810
My Fortress Whale Deck will swallow them up!

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.240
When it comes to size, my Dinosaur Deck is no slouch!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.800
Enough of your nonsense!

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:36.110
My Fortress Whale is cyborg-ized to fly!

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.320
Other than Great Moth, my deck has-

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.720
Oops, it's a secret.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.110
You've gone too far to stop talking!

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.120
They tire me out.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:03.750
Yugi Muto and Mai Kujaku.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.150
They have excellent rare cards.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.240
My starting point is at the east side of the city.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.140
Mine is the ocean!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.300
See ya!

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.520
Yugi, I'm going too.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.380
Let's meet at the finals.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.520
Yeah!

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.930
This is my starting location.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.280
Kaiba should be announcing the tournament soon.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.740
How's he going to do that here?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.680
Duelists!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.600
Welcome to Battle City!

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.670
That's Kaiba's voice!

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.390
Where is he?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.540
Where?

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.880
Where's it coming from?

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.100
Kaiba!

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.100
I'll explain the rules.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:21.120
The participants in the city are duelists that Kaiba Corporation has certified as level 5 and above.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:26.020
Having a Duel Disk proves that.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:29.840
The tournament takes place throughout Domino City.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:35.020
If you encounter a duelist anywhere in the city, that's where you will duel.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.390
Throughout the city?

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:42.170
Duelists will use their own 40-card decks.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:46.440
The loser must give one rare card to the winner.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:52.450
In Battle City, the more you win, the stronger your deck becomes.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.530
The ante rule.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:59.100
Duelists never want to lose a rare card.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.140
I can't afford to lose.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:05.650
This tournament will be a fierce battle.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:11.660
Only eight participants who survive the battle royal will make the finals.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.270
Eight?

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:19.500
The finals will take place in a secret location somewhere in the city.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.500
Secret location?

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:27.510
I'm also participating in this tournament under the same rules as you.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.920
So I don't know the location of the finals either.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.350
What's that mean?

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.850
How can we find the location?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.850
Look at your plate that shows your starting location.

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:41.620
This plate is a Puzzle Card.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.860
If you stack the Cards, it will create a map of Domino City.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.360
Each Puzzle Card has a special prism.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:54.870
When you stack six cards, the whole map appears.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.450
A light will shine on one spot.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.610
That's the location of the finals.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:04.600
You will wager your Puzzle Cards in your duels.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:12.060
Only those who gather six Puzzle Cards can go to the hidden location for the finals.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.600
Hidden location for the finals...

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.380
I promise...

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:18.380
...to get there!

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.100
Battle City will now begin!

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:26.330
Duelists, go find your opponents in the city!

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.840
Okay, I can't dilly-dally either!

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.380
Jonouchi!

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.530
Who shall be my first prey...

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:46.390
I finally found you!

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:54.630
I knew you'd show up in Battle City!

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.330
Well, well.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:02.060
Even if you try to hide in a crowd, you can't fool me!

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:33.370
So even a loser dog can't stop barking.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.240
Loser dog?

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.800
Don't call me that!

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.040
It makes me angry!

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.280
Jonouchi!

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:42.750
Yugi!

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:44.800
Yugi Muto.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:45.980
Perfect timing.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:48.860
He stole my Red-Eyes!

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:54.720
He's a Ghoul, a member of the dark syndicate that controls underground gaming.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.970
Yugi, don't deal with this punk!

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:10.970
You want to duel me again even though your deck doesn't have Red-Eyes?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:17.290
But I don't want to deal with you because you don't have a rare card.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.810
Yugi Muto, you're my opponent!

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:22.310
Wait!  This is my problem!

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:25.320
No.  I accept this duel!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:26.320
Yugi.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:31.500
Those who steal a duelist's irreplaceable card...

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.300
...will not be forgiven!

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:47.570
I'll clean up trash like you that pollute this city!

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:52.580
You'll never defeat my Exodia deck.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:56.600
Yugi, they do whatever it takes to win.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:13:02.090
They create counterfeit rare cards to build the strongest decks.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.020
And his deck contains-

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:07.330
Say no more, Jonouchi!

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.060
But...

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:15.170
No matter how dirty he is, I have no right to know his cards before the duel.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.910
Rare Hunter!

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:21.180
Come at me with your best tactics!

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.180
My deck will destroy you head-on!

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.680
Yugi...

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:30.820
How admirable of you.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.220
But that's enough to win the duel!

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:40.690
Your naïve sense of justice won't work against the Ghouls!

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:46.700
You'll lose your rare cards and fall into the darkness known as defeat!

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:49.700
We'll see about that.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:55.270
Where is he?

00:13:57.470 --> 00:14:01.720
The tournament is in the city, but where am I supposed to look?

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.750
Launch Solid Vision System!

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:28.000
Brother, the first duel is starting.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:30.670
It's Yugi!

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:32.000
Yugi is dueling!

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.240
So Yugi is going to start.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.250
I'll watch for a while.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.250
Let's keep searching for the God Cards.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:45.110
The duelist with the two remaining God Cards must be somewhere.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:48.860
Thoroughly check the data sent from the Duel Disks!

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.910
Duel!

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:54.370
I'll go first.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.440
I draw!

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:01.950
I'm starting with two Exodia cards in my hand.

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:07.450
When I have all five cards, I win.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:13.480
Yugi, please figure out his strategy!

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:14.770
Here I go!

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:17.510
I set two cards on the field.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:22.350
Beta The Magnet Warrior in attack position!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.600
I end my turn.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.360
What is that?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.800
A weird thing came out of a card.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.800
That's Duel Monsters.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:37.620
Starting today, duelists will tear through this city!

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.260
My turn.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:41.210
I draw.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:43.620
Graceful Charity.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.850
I draw three cards from my deck.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.440
I discard two.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.660
I now have three parts.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.900
That card replaces his hand.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.740
He's up to something.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.180
In that case, I flip over my trap card!

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:07.700
Light of Intervention!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:13.580
As long as this trap card is active, all monsters must be faceup.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.720
That's pointless.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.960
Stone Statue of the Aztecs in defense position.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.800
A monster in defense.

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:31.460
I can't damage his life points unless I destroy that monster.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.200
My turn!

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:37.850
I tribute Beta The Magnet Warrior to summon Berfomet!

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:44.400
Due to Berfomet's effect, I summon Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.550
Then I flip over my set card!

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:52.680
I use Polymerization to fuse my two monsters.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:02.380
I summon the Fusion Monster Chimera the Flying Mythical Beast!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:11.640
Under Battle City rules, Fusion Monsters can't attack until the next turn.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:17.080
But my Chimera will destroy your defending monster!

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.240
No, Yugi!

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.310
Forget about the monsters on his field!

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:24.820
He's gathering Exodia cards in his hand.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:30.570
Keep focusing on those monster battles.

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:35.390
Meanwhile, I'll collect the remaining Exodia parts.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.670
You'll lose without knowing it.

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:44.100
I set a card and end my turn.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.840
My turn.  I draw.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.440
The spell card Graceful Charity.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:55.350
I draw three cards and discard two.

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:57.700
He replaced his hand again.

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:05.070
My deck contains three copies of each Exodia part.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:07.130
I've gathered four parts.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:11.130
I only need Left Arm of the Forbidden One.

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:14.120
What's he up to?

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:20.600
He uses a strange strategy.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:21.670
Seto.

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:25.370
The cards he's playing haven't been registered.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.320
What?  Are they God Cards?

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:29.950
No, they're counterfeit cards.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:30.820
What?

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.620
He's a Ghoul.

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:36.040
Big brother!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.020
Wait!

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.610
Interesting.  Let him play.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.960
I figured out his deck type.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.380
Keep thinking.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:58.120
Your time is running out anyway.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:03.280
With my special contact lenses, I can see the invisible paint on the back of my cards.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.090
So I know which card is at the top of my deck.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:12.090
I will draw Left Arm of the Forbidden One on my next turn!

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:15.090
Exodia will be completed!

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.730
There's no way you can win!

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:22.270
Every strategy is powerless against Exodia!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:23.880
Yugi...

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:31.530
I summon Gear Golem the Moving Fortress in defense position.

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:35.280
I end my turn.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.280
Another monster to defend with?  Why?

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:41.790
I don't feel like he wants to attack.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:47.100
He only strengthens his defenses to protect himself from my monsters.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:51.960
He's not thinking of monster battles to take away my life points.

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:55.200
What's wrong?  It's your turn.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.720
So how is he going to defeat me?

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:00.710
How can he defeat me without attacking?

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:03.580
Yugi!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.450
Yugi, you shouldn't be having this duel!

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:10.160
You can't have a fair duel against a Ghoul!

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:11.840
You're wrong, Jonouchi.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:17.190
I'll fight fair and square to the end and defeat him.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:22.760
A true duelist never leaves the battlefield, no matter who the opponent is.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.560
Yugi...

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:29.470
Jonouchi, I promise to win for you!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:34.370
You risked your life to save my cards before.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:37.380
I'll now pay back that debt!

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:40.650
Replacing his hand...

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.370
Creating card copies...

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:46.050
I see what he can do.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:49.510
I've figured out what you're trying to do!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:54.460
I won't let you summon Exodia!

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.630
What?  He figured out my strategy?

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:58.860
Yugi!

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:03.870
Jonouchi, you helped me figure out his strategy.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:11.260
Even though you figured out my strategy, you have no time left.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:15.460
I already have most of the Exodia cards in my hand.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.480
It's too late to do anything.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.290
Interesting.

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:25.590
I wonder if you can actually control Exodia.

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:45.860
Yugi figured out that the Rare Hunter's strategy is to summon Exodia.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:52.360
But the Rare Hunter is prepared for Yugi's anti-Exodia strategy and stops Yugi's attacks.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:57.930
If Yugi doesn't finish him before he gathers all the Exodia parts, Yugi will lose!

00:21:57.930 --> 00:22:01.060
Is there a way to turn the tables?

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:04.330
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Comeback  Chain Destruction

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:05.960
Duel, standby!

00:22:20.830 --> 00:22:25.330
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:30.700
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:40.380
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:51.890
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:59.400
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:04.670
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:09.780
Will never change

00:23:10.440 --> 00:23:15.050
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:20.250
To be who I am

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:25.490
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.160 --> 00:23:30.200
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:33.130
I learned that's the answer

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:40.240
From now until forever...
